","The APPELLANT assailed the judgment and order dated 15.06.2023 of the Divisional Special Judge, Chattogram in a special case arising out of a police station case of 2019, by which he was found guilty under section 161 of the Penal Code and section 5(2) of the Prevention of Corruption Act, 1947 and sentenced to concurrent terms of imprisonment with fines. The prosecution alleged that the APPELLANT, then an upazila education officer, demanded money from an assistant teacher for forwarding the proposal for her transfer, received a part of it, and was caught with marked notes by a trap committee. The defence contended that no money was taken, that the proposal had in fact been forwarded earlier, that the witnesses to the seizure did not support the case, and that the departmental proceeding had ended without any finding against him.",Penal Code 1860,ALLOWED,"The court held that conscious acceptance of the money by the public servant had to be proved, and found from the evidence that the upazila education officer had approved and forwarded the proposal for transfer well before the alleged demand, so there was no reason to demand money days later. It found that the witness who was present saw no exchange of money and said the APPELLANT refused to accept what was offered, that the seizure witnesses did not support the transaction, that the notes themselves were not produced, and that the investigating officer was withheld. The trial court had ignored the written statement and papers submitted by the accused.",8c05e77da5eee5a0aeeb645ffc8e5d6c63e3a95aae544defb1678424f12aec4f
