","The PETITIONERS, defendants in a title suit, assailed the judgment and decree dated 30.01.2023 of the Joint District Judge, First Court, Barishal in a title appeal, by which the appellate court dealt with the appeal against the judgment and decree dated 28.01.2008 of the Senior Assistant Judge, Sadar, Barishal in the title suit. That suit had been brought by the OPPOSITE PARTIES for a declaration that a decree passed in their absence in an earlier title suit was collusive, fraudulent and not binding on them, pleading that the land had been conveyed to their predecessor and others by a registered deed of gift in exchange long before that suit, in which they had not been impleaded. The PETITIONERS pleaded an oral gift in their favour and the latest record in their name, and disputed the deed relied on by the OPPOSITE PARTIES.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court found that the registered deed of gift in exchange produced by the OPPOSITE PARTIES, and proved through a witness examined before the appellate court, showed a transfer of the holding to them and two others long before the earlier suit was brought, and that they were admittedly not impleaded in it although their application to be added as defendants in that suit had itself been turned down. It held that a decree on title and possession of immovable property binds only the parties to the suit, and that in a suit of this nature only locus standi and a reasonable interest need be shown.",9188556fe832967bc4019c5244df1a3fa8b7e244e56b44a5d604a72ced6adcf9
