With this observation and direction, the instant rule is disposed of. 
Communicate the order at once. 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
                (Mamnoon Rahman,J:) 
","In this revisional application the PETITIONERS were the plaintiffs in a pending suit concerning a disputed holding over which an order restraining the OPPOSITE PARTIES from carrying on works on the land had been made during the pendency of the proceeding, and that order was later displaced in appeal at the instance of the defendants. The PETITIONERS came to this Court under the revisional jurisdiction, and the OPPOSITE PARTIES contested the matter. This Court considered that the interlocutory dispute had already consumed considerable time and that the controversy could only be settled finally by a decision of the suit on its own merits rather than by prolonging interim arrangements.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,PARTLY,"UNCERTAIN: the Rule was closed with a direction only, without deciding the correctness of the appellate order, so the classification is doubtful. The court took the view, shared by the parties, that justice would be served if the trial court were directed to hear and dispose of the suit expeditiously within a fixed period rather than by keeping the interlocutory order under scrutiny. It accordingly directed that the suit be heard and decided strictly on merit by applying independent and judicial mind within the time fixed, without any adjournment, and ordered that until then both sides maintain status quo in respect of the possession and position of the property in dispute.",1f8d01a43535e25b118e5308d2770a08510f60f220a6b16b0d57962bf2533199
