IN THE SUPREME COURT OF BANGLADESH 
 
 
 
 
   HIGH COURT DIVISION 
 
 
        (CIVIL APPELLATE JURISDICTION) 
 
 
 
First Miscellaneous Appeal No. 133 of 2024 
With 
Civil Rule No. 64(fm)/2024 
 
 
 
 
 
 
In the matter of: 
 
Mohammed Rejaul Kader and others. 
 
 
...Appellants. 
 
 
 
 
 
-Vs- 
Enayet Ullah. 
 
 
....Respondent. 
 
 
 
None appears.  
 
 
 
 
       …For the appellants. 
 
 
 
Mr. Samarendra Nath Biswas, Adv. 
 
 
 
 
…For the respondent-opposite party. 
 
 
 
 
Heard on: 06.01.2025 
And 
Judgment on: The 7th January, 2025 
 
Mamnoon Rahman,J: 
 
Both the appeal as well as rule are heard together as the similar 
question of fact and law are involved in it as well as the parties are 
same and now disposed of by a single judgment. 
 
This appeal is directed against the judgment and order dated 
13.02.2024 passed by the learned Joint District Judge, 2nd Court, Feni 
in Title Suit No. 22 of 2023 rejecting the application under Order 39 
rule 1 along with section 151 of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908 for 
temporary injunction. 
I have heard the learned Advocate for the respondent. I have 
perused the Memorandum of appeal, grounds taken thereon, 
application for injunction, as well as necessary papers and documents 
annexed herewith. 

<<PAGE 2>>
On perusal of the same, it transpires that the Title Suit being 
No. 22 of 2023 pending before the court below and arising out of 
which the instant appeal was preferred before this court regarding an 
interim order. It further transpires that at the time of admission of 
appeal as well as rule this court passed an order of status-quo in 
respect of possession and position of the suit land.  
Considering the facts and circumstances, I am of the view that 
justice would be done if a direction be given upon the court below to 
hear and dispose of the suit expeditiously, as possible, within a fixed 
date. Accordingly, the court below is directed to hear and dispose of 
the suit strictly on merit by applying its independent and judicial mind 
within 30th June, 2025 without fail and without giving any 
adjournment to the parties. The court below is further directed to 
inform this court about the disposal of the suit as directed, in writing, 
through the Registrar of the High Court Division within 7(seven) days 
from the date of disposal of the suit. 
Since the order of status-quo is continuing from 04.03.2024 I 
am of the view that the same be continued for the period as directed 
by this court regarding disposal of the suit. 
With this observation and direction, the instant appeal being 
No. 133 of 2024 as well as the connected Rule being No. 64(fm) of 
2024 are disposed of. 
The office is directed to communicate the order to the 
concerned court below with a copy of the judgment, at once. 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
                (Mamnoon Rahman,J:) 
","The APPELLANTS, defendants in a title suit, assailed the order of the Joint District Judge rejecting their application under Order XXXIX rule 1 with section 151 of the Code of Civil Procedure for a temporary injunction, and the connected Rule was heard with the appeal as the parties and the questions were the same. The OPPOSITE PARTY, the plaintiff, contested the appeal, while no one appeared for the appellants at the hearing. At the time of admission of the appeal and the Rule this Court had made an order of status quo in respect of the possession and position of the suit land, which had continued since then, and it considered whether that arrangement should be kept alive.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,PARTLY,"UNCERTAIN: the appeal was disposed of with a direction, the order under challenge not having been decided on its merits, so the classification is doubtful. The court observed that the suit was pending and that the appeal and connected Rule arose out of an interim order passed in it, and took the view that justice would be done if the trial court were directed to hear and dispose of the suit expeditiously within a fixed date rather than by entertaining the interlocutory challenge further. It directed disposal of the suit strictly on merit without adjournments, required a report of the disposal through the Registrar, and continued the order of status quo until the suit was decided.",0360356d60c7d3d729a0dc4b7853f1446b94f13240dbd68782a29b6c1fbea692
2500-2513,Criminal Appeal No. 1521 of 2020,2025-01-09,"
<<PAGE 1>>
1 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
ABO Hasan 
IN THE SUPREME COURT OF 
BANGLADESH 
HIGH COURT DIVISION 
   (CRIMINAL APPELLATE JURISDICTION) 
Present: 
Mr. Justice Md. Shohrowardi 
Criminal Appeal No. 1521 of 2020 
Md. Monaem Hossain @ Md. 
Mounayem Hossain  
………Appellant  
-Vs- 
The State and another 
….respondents  
     Mr. Abdullah Al Rasel, Advocate 
 ….For the appellant  
Mr. Farhad Hossain Siddique, 
