","The petitioner moved this Division in revision against an order of the District Judge passed in a miscellaneous appeal, by which the appellate court had appointed a receiver over the property in dispute and had reversed an order of the Joint District Judge declining such appointment in a long-pending partition suit. The petitioners contended that the appointment was not warranted in the facts and circumstances of the case. At the hearing, the learned advocates appearing for the petitioners and for the opposite parties stated that, in the meantime, the execution case arising out of the final decree in the partition suit had been disposed of on satisfaction.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court perused the impugned order, the revisional application, the grounds taken and the documents annexed, and considered the statement made at the bar by the learned advocates of both sides. Since the execution case had already been disposed of on satisfaction by execution of the final decree in the partition suit, the appointment of receiver that the petitioners were challenging no longer retained any operative force, and no cause of action subsisted for maintaining it. The court held that the revisional rule had lost its purpose and therefore declined it as infructuous, without any order as to costs.",23c6bf4083ed525cf9247ca1c92ff73a4223da7e09a38a4e4cdec2aa53931121
