","A rule was issued in this civil revision at the instance of the petitioners, calling upon certain opposite parties to show cause why an error appearing in the record of the case should not be rectified. The controversy concerned the substitution of heirs following the death of one of the opposite parties during the pendency of the revision, it being asserted that the heirs of the deceased had been wrongly brought on record in place of another set of heirs. A correction application invoking the statutory provision relating to the amendment of mistakes in judgments and orders was filed, and the matter was taken up for hearing. None appeared for the opposite parties when it was called on.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,ALLOWED,"The court perused the application for modification and correction as well as the grounds taken in support of it. On examination it appeared that the record did contain a bona fide mistake in the matter of substitution, the heirs of the deceased opposite party having been shown wrongly in place of the correct set of heirs. The court found substance in the rule, and permitting the correction application so far as it related to substitution, ordered that the correct heirs of the deceased opposite party be brought on record in place of those erroneously shown. No view was expressed on the merits of the underlying revision, which was left to be heard separately.",1c041da8ac37cefa0c91476a489fbe5f03ea48b103959681a0a0c3e7c2c3233d
