Emdad. B.O. 
","The petitioner had moved this Division in the year 1990 with an application for transfer of a title suit then pending in the court of an Assistant Judge, praying that the suit be withdrawn from that court and tried either by this Division or by some other competent court of the same district. On that application a rule had been issued and an interim order made. When the matter eventually came on for hearing, no one appeared on behalf of either of the parties, and the court was left to consider the record as it stood.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court observed that the application for transfer had been pressed in 1990 and that a quarter of a century had since elapsed, with the result that the cause of action on which the prayer rested no longer subsisted. No reason was found for interfering with the pending proceeding. The rule accordingly did not succeed, and no order as to costs was made, and the interim order passed at the time of its issuance was vacated. The trial court was, however, directed to proceed with the suit expeditiously and in accordance with law. No finding on the merits of the suit itself was recorded.",2fd6f2ee0cc329dfdf37c0e9bf95d00906e5689022b84b3bac30457d8a7d5799
