In an application under section 115(1) of the Code of Civil 
Procedure, 1908 rule was issued calling upon the opposite party to 
show cause as to why the impugned judgment and order dated 
01.02.2023 passed by the learned District Judge, Dhaka allowing the 
Arbitration Miscellaneous Case No. 441 of 2022 under section 12 of 
the Arbitration Act, 2001, and thereby, appointing Arbitrators on behalf 
of the parties for settlement of the dispute of the case through 
arbitration should not be set aside and/or pass such other or further 
order or orders as to this court may seem fit and proper. 
 
I have heard the learned Advocates for the petitioner as well as 
opposite parties. I have perused the impugned judgment and order 
passed by the court below, perused the revisional application, ground 
taken thereon as well as necessary papers and documents annexed 
herewith. 
   Present  
          Mr. Justice Mamnoon Rahman 
 
 
 
 

<<PAGE 2>>
At the very outset both the parties agreed that if a sole Arbitrator 
is being appointed by this court they have no objection to that effect 
and both the parties unanimously suggested the name of Justice 
Moyeenul Islam Chowdhury to act as sole Arbitrator to resolve the 
issue in question.  
Considering the facts and circumstances, Mr. Justice Moyeenul 
Islam Chowdhury, Former Judge, High Court Division of the Supreme 
Court of Bangladesh is appointed as sole Arbitrator to conduct the 
arbitration in question. 
Accordingly, the instant rule is disposed of. The order of stay 
passed at the time of issuance of rule is hereby vacated. 
Send down the L.C. Records to the concerned court below with a 
copy of the judgment immediately. Communicate the order at once. 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
