","The petitioners challenged before this Division an order of the District Judge by which a miscellaneous case was disposed of and arbitrators were appointed on behalf of the parties for settlement of their dispute through arbitration. The revision was filed under the revisional provision of the Code of Civil Procedure, and a stay had been ordered at the time of issuance of the rule. When the matter was taken up, both parties stated at the very outset that they had no objection to the appointment of a sole arbitrator by this court, and they jointly suggested the name of a retired judge of this Division for that purpose.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,PARTLY,"Having heard the learned advocates of both sides and perused the impugned order, the grounds taken and the annexed papers, the court accepted the joint submission made at the bar. The retired judge suggested by both parties was appointed sole arbitrator to conduct the arbitration in question, so that the dispute between them would be resolved through that process rather than through the mechanism earlier put in place by the court below. The revisional rule was accordingly disposed of, the stay earlier ordered being vacated, and the lower court records were directed to be sent down with a copy of the judgment.",f20bbb73bf9adb38feb316c56e95204c25c266b04b0ce1f855c969567740504c
