Obaidul Hasan/B.O. 
","This civil revision had been carried to this Division against concurrent decisions of the courts below in a long-pending civil litigation between the parties. When the matter reached hearing, the learned advocate for the petitioners stated that both the petitioners had died long before, and that their heirs were not interested either in being substituted in their place or in pursuing the revisional rule. Counsel for the first opposite party, the contesting defendant below, informed the court that this opposite party had also died and that his heirs too were unwilling to contest the rule any further.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court took note of the information furnished by the learned advocates of both sides and observed that proceedings cannot be carried on for or against persons who are dead. Since none of the heirs of either set of parties had come forward to be brought on record or to pursue the matter, there was no party before the court competent to continue the litigation, and no useful purpose would be served by keeping the revisional rule pending. In the circumstances the rule was not pressed to a decision on merit and was brought to an end, the court making no order as to costs and directing the records to be sent down.",dcf8a28052abf5e280ca2bfc18c258ab398d6859ff63e36172d6135e4e36e6f0
